#
# prima-materia — Transerfing: the tradition and its works
#
# The tradition is registered and entered in the same run (prima-materia#924):
# it stood in no registry before. This file declares the tradition, the five
# Stupeni and Tufti; the harvest of each Stupen' stands in its own file,
# traditions/transerfing-stupen-<n>.ttl.
#
# Identifiers: Transerfing plus the Russian term of the system in a plain
# Latin transliteration where the term is fixed in Russian usage (Mayatnik,
# IzbytochnyPotentsial, Vazhnost), otherwise a short English term for what the
# translation describes.
#

pmw:TranserfingStupen1 a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov"@en, "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti. Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov, first published by Ves, St Petersburg, 2004. Read whole on 2026-11-13, foreword and chapters I to VI, in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012, ISBN 978-5-9573-2880-3), whose chapters I to XIX run through the five Stupeni; the translator is not named in the text layer. Full text of the Internet Archive identifier reality-transurfing-steps-i-v-vadim-zeland (1704368 bytes, ASCII letter share 1.0, not access-restricted); the text layer carries no page numbers, so places are cited by chapter and section heading."@en ;
    skos:note "That chapters I to VI of the combined edition are this Stupen' rests on a second translation: the Bulgarian Пространство на варианти under the Internet Archive identifier knigi-zip-prostranstvo-na-varianti-vadim-zeland (331508 characters, open; translator and edition not named in the text layer), which carries the foreword and chapters I to VI with the same titles (Модел на вариантите to Течение на вариантите) and ends with the summary of chapter VI. The Bulgarian was held against the English at the reception passage (the dream of the keeper of the reserve, Надзирателя на резервата, chapter I; the English gives him a grey beard, the Bulgarian a white one) and at the chapter distribution of the system terms (махало from chapter II, излишен потенциал and важност from chapter IV, индуциран преход chapter V, течение на вариантите chapter VI), and agrees at both; nothing else was compared; whether the combined edition of 2011/2012 revised the wording of 2004 was not checked, because the Russian scans are access-restricted."@en .

pmw:TranserfingStupen2 a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd"@en, "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti. Stupen' II: Shelest utrennikh zvezd (Ves, 2004). Not opened in this run. On 2026-11-13 the Russian scan transerfingrealn0000zela_s5v8 was access-restricted; open are the English combined edition (reality-transurfing-steps-i-v-vadim-zeland, from chapter VII, Intention) and a Bulgarian translation, Шепотът на утринните звезди (knigi-zip-shepotat-na-utrinnite-zvezdi-vadim-zeland)."@en .

pmw:TranserfingStupen3 a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe!"@en, "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe!"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti. Stupen' III: Vpered v proshloe! (Ves, 2004). Not opened in this run. On 2026-11-13 the Russian scan bwb_P6-BZN-002 was access-restricted; open are the English combined edition and a Bulgarian translation, Напред в миналото (knigi-zip-napred-v-minaloto-vadim-zeland)."@en .

pmw:TranserfingStupen4 a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu"@en, "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti. Stupen' IV: Upravlenie real'nost'yu (Ves, 2005). Not opened in this run. On 2026-11-13 the Russian scan transerfingrealn0000zela_h1t0 was access-restricted; open is the English combined edition."@en .

pmw:TranserfingStupen5 a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo"@en, "Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti. Stupen' V: Yabloki padayut v nebo (Ves, 2005 or 2006). Not opened in this run. On 2026-11-13 the Russian scan transerfingreano0000zela was access-restricted; open are the English combined edition and a Bulgarian translation, Ябълките падат в небето (knigi-zip-yabalkite-padat-v-nebeto-vadim-zeland)."@en .

pmw:TranserfingZhritsaItfat a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "Zhritsa Itfat (Tufti)"@en, "Zhritsa Itfat (Tufti)"@de ;
    skos:note "Vadim Zeland, Zhritsa Itfat (2018), English as Tufti the Priestess. Not opened in this run; the Internet Archive search of 2026-11-13 found a Bulgarian translation, Жрицата Тафти (knigi-zip-zhritsata-tafti-vadim-zeland), and no Russian or English text layer."@en .

pmt:Transerfing a pm:Tradition ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    rdfs:label "Transerfing"@en, "Transerfing"@de ;
    skos:definition "The transmission of a model of reality as a space of alternatives through which a person moves by intention, together with a body of practice for lowering the importance one attaches to things, freeing oneself of collective energy structures and selecting one's own life line, carried in the books of Vadim Zeland from 2004 and the courses and readers that follow them."@en ;
    skos:note "A young transmission, registered and entered in the same run on 2026-11-13 under prima-materia#924. The author names no teacher and no lineage; the account that he was a quantum physicist is his own and stands as that. Who stands behind the name is not settled in the works read."@en ;
    skos:note "The first of the three decisions SPEC §14 asks for, the contact route, is documented, against the recommendation of prima-materia#924, which expected none. Stupen' I names no source; the combined edition does, outside it: chapter XVII (The Dreams of the Gods) says the books of Carlos Castaneda and Theun Mares describe a model of human perception, gives the Toltec cocoon and assemblage point, and combines that model with Transerfing; chapter XVI cites Castaneda for shifting the assemblage point; chapter XV calls a burst of laughter Castaneda-like. Agreement between Transerfing and pmt:CastanedaToltec on intention, importance or perception is therefore reception and counts once. The likeness to pmt:NewThought (thought as radiation that materialises circumstances) has no named route in the works read and is not a convergence either until one is entered as pm:Converging with pm:compilerInference."@en ;
    skos:note "The second decision, recension and edition: the English translation of the combined edition of 2012, the only open carrier with the whole text; the Russian scans of 2004 to 2011 are access-restricted, and whether the combined edition revised the single volumes was not checked. The third, the number of citable places: Stupen' I has a foreword and six chapters with about fifty headed sections and a summary list at the end of each chapter, cited by chapter and section."@en ;
    skos:note "What the harvest of Stupen' I found, in counts (traditions/transerfing-stupen-1.ttl, 698 nodes): 96 practices, 93 yieldings, 33 chains of which 18 stated necessities with the consequence of skipping, 2 series, 68 cautions, 68 conditions of failure, 26 signs of success announced in advance, 6 namings, 1 receiving, 14 orderings by the author. The conditions of failure lie almost all at the practitioner: excess potential, importance, struggle and dependence on pendulums undo the outcome, and the balancing forces are named as the mechanism. No deadline after which an operation counts as failed, and no rate."@en ;
    skos:note "Open, and the next places to go: Stupeni II to V, read in the same combined edition from chapter VII (Intention) on, with the Bulgarian translations of II, III and V as second witnesses; Zhritsa Itfat, for which only a Bulgarian translation was found."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupeni I-V (2004-2006); Zhritsa Itfat (2018)" ;
    pm:corpusWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1, pmw:TranserfingStupen2, pmw:TranserfingStupen3, pmw:TranserfingStupen4, pmw:TranserfingStupen5, pmw:TranserfingZhritsaItfat ;
    pm:coverageState pm:placesEntered ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteDocumented ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), foreword and chapters I-VI; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named" .
